* sg13g2-lna -- supply-ramp startup / latch check of the Option-A
* bias-reference skeleton (issue #33 / DR-0003; the ramp convention is
* the committed sim/lna-bias-pvt one).
* Generated from sim/biasref-topology/testbench/tb_core_startup.spice.tmpl
* by sim/biasref-topology/run_biasref_sweep.sh -- do not edit a generated
* file directly, edit this template and re-run.
*
* Generated for: MOS_SECTION=@@MOS_SECTION@@ HBT_SECTION=@@HBT_SECTION@@
* TEMP=@@TEMP@@ C VDD=@@VDD@@ V
*
* WHY THIS EXISTS: unlike the committed mirror feed (a plain R3a branch
* from vdd -- deliberately feedforward, no degenerate state), the Option-A
* skeleton is a self-biased PTAT loop, and that loop's zero-current state
* is a genuine degenerate operating point (the classic bandgap startup
* surface). The seed leg (Rseed) is the committed-design answer: a
* 10 Meg pull-up on the plain-diode leg's node guarantees a nonzero
* bootstrap current. This deck demonstrates that numerically the same
* way sim/lna-bias-pvt/testbench/tb_lna_startup.spice.tmpl does for the
* committed family: VDD ramps 0 V -> target in 1 us (slow vs. any circuit
* pole), holds to 12 us, and the runner checks that the island current's
* last samples agree with each other (settled, not ringing) and match the
* same cell's op-value (no latch to a different stable state).
*
* Cells: the same three the committed 45-cell startup check uses --
* bcs/125 C/1.98 V, wcs/-40 C/1.62 V, typ/27 C/1.80 V.

.lib "@@MODELS_LIB@@" @@HBT_SECTION@@
.lib "@@MOS_LIB@@" @@MOS_SECTION@@
.options temp=@@TEMP@@ tnom=27

Vvdd vdd 0 pwl(0 0 1e-6 @@VDD@@ 1.2e-5 @@VDD@@)
Vssa vss 0 dc 0

XMb nc_b nc_b vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XQb nc_b nc_a nc_e vss npn13G2 Nx=8
Rp  nc_e vss 3.4k
XMa nc_a nc_b vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XQa nc_a nc_a vss vss npn13G2 Nx=1
Rseed vdd nc_a 10meg
XMk bref nc_b vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=210u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XQ3 bref bref vss vss npn13G2 Nx=1

